      "message": "\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDon\u0027t fail metric computation due to duplicated metric names The jgit/block_cache/cache_used_per_repository metric can produce\u003cbr\u003eduplicate metric names, since it uses the repository path, where\u003cbr\u003eslashes are replaced with hyphens as a field, e.g.:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003erepo1: /gerrit/git/test-abcd.git\u003cbr\u003erepo2: /gerrit/git/test/abcd.git\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ewould lead to the same metric name:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ejgit/block_cache/cache_used_per_repository/-gerrit-git-test-abcd.git\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e!!! THIS BUG TRACKER IS FOR GERRIT CODE REVIEW !!!!\u003cbr\u003e*** Do not submit bugs for chrome/android and issues with your company\u0027s\u003cbr\u003e*** Gerrit setup here. Those issues belong in different issue trackers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:separator --\u003e\n\u003chr class\u003d\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:separator --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat steps will reproduce the problem?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} --\u003e\n\u003col class\u003d\"wp-block-list\"\u003e\u003c!-- wp:list-item --\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate a repository foo/bar\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list-item --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:list-item --\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate a repository foo-bar\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list-item --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:list-item --\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInstall metrics-reporter-prometheus\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list-item --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:list-item --\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ecreate some changes for clone foo/bar, and for foo-bar in order to populate the jgit cache\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list-item --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:list-item --\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ehit the metrics reporter prometheus endpoint\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list-item --\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ecurl -s -H\u0027Authorization: Bearer token123\u0027 \u0027http://localhost:8080/plugins/metrics-reporter-prometheus/metrics\u0027\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat is the expected output?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince the repository names are ambiguous this should be logged and no repository metrics should be exposed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat do you see instead?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAn exception is thrown:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e[HTTP-93] WARN org.eclipse.jetty.server.HttpChannel : /plugins/metrics-reporter-prometheus/metrics\u003cbr\u003ejava.lang.IllegalArgumentException: A metric named jgit/block_cache/cache_used_per_repository/-Users-syntonyze-ginstall-gerrit-2.16.28-git-foo-bar.git already exists\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease provide any additional information below\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eModify \u0027sanitizeMetricName\u0027 to avoid collisions\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt present there is a simple \u0027DropWizardMetricMaker.sanitizeMetricName\u0027\u003cbr\u003eimplementation that:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:list --\u003e\n\u003cul class\u003d\"wp-block-list\"\u003e\u003c!-- wp:list-item --\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ereplaces the leading \u003ccode\u003e/\u003c/code\u003e with \u003ccode\u003e_\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list-item --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:list-item --\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ereduces the repeated \u003ccode\u003e/\u003c/code\u003e chars to a single \u003ccode\u003e/\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list-item --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:list-item --\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eremoves the ending \u003ccode\u003e/\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list-item --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:list-item --\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ereplaces not supported chars with \u003ccode\u003e_\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list-item --\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs a result of collision between the sanitized metric names can be easy\u003cbr\u003ecreated e.g. \u003ccode\u003efoo_bar\u003c/code\u003e will collide with \u003ccode\u003efoo+bar\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn order to avoid collisions keep the rules about slashes (they are\u003cbr\u003eneeded anyway) and:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:list --\u003e\n\u003cul class\u003d\"wp-block-list\"\u003e\u003c!-- wp:list-item --\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ereplace not supported chars with \u003ccode\u003e_0x[HEX CODE]_\u003c/code\u003e string (code is\u003cbr\u003ecapitalized)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list-item --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:list-item --\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ethe replacement prefix \u003ccode\u003e0x\u003c/code\u003e is prepended with another replacement\u003cbr\u003eprefix\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list-item --\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:list --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs a result:\u003cbr\u003e\u003ccode\u003efoo_bar\u003c/code\u003e stays \u003ccode\u003efoo_bar\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003ccode\u003efoo+bar\u003c/code\u003e becomes \u003ccode\u003efoo_0x2B_bar\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003ccode\u003efoo_0x2B_bar\u003c/code\u003e becomes \u003ccode\u003efoo_0x_0x2B_bar\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003eand collision is no longer possible\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe replace algorithm was inspired by the work done in If11e6576eff\u003cbr\u003e(…..to….).\u003cbr\u003eProblems arise when file paths are included directly in metric names. This practice creates what\u0027s known as a high cardinality problem.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHigh cardinality occurs because each unique file path (e.g., C:\\app\\logs\\file1.log, C:\\app\\logs\\file2.log, and so on) generates an entirely new metric. If a system has thousands or even millions of files, this can overwhelm the monitoring system with too many unique metrics.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProblem Fix:\u003cbr\u003eMetrics are data collected to measure the performance or behavior of a system (e.g., memory usage or the number of requests processed).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProblems arise when file paths are included directly in the metric name. This practice creates what is known as a high cardinality problem.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHigh cardinality occurs because each unique file path (e.g., C:\\app\\logs\\file1.log, C:\\app\\logs\\file2.log, and so on) generates an entirely new metric. If a system has thousands or even millions of files, this can overwhelm the monitoring system with too many unique metrics.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImpact and Fixes\u003cbr\u003eHigh cardinality can cause several serious problems:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMemory Consumption: The monitoring system must store each unique metric name, which can consume a significant amount of memory.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePoor Performance: Querying or aggregating metric data becomes very slow and inefficient.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInstability: Excessive load can cause the monitoring system to become unstable or even crash.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTherefore, this fix aims to remove or replace file paths with more common and consistent names within the metrics. This way, metrics will be grouped appropriately, reducing the number of unique metrics, and improving the overall efficiency and reliability of metric computation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA small example of my account C2/cc\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\n1.Duplicate/fake status / sync without confirmation https://android-review.googlesource.com/q/owner:campaeciax@gmail.com\n\n2 real accounts https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/cts/+/comments/https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/cts/+comment\n\n\n\n\u003c!-- wp:paragraph --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWho owns this ID 980-g607fd889b8? Is he the owner of this Gerrit forum?\u003cbr\u003eIf so, why doesn\u0027t he use his own facilities?\u003cbr\u003eWhy does he have to attach them to someone else\u0027s Android device?\u003cbr\u003eBecause as far as I know, the owner of a discussion forum, especially a prestigious one like this, must have a high level of understanding. So it\u0027s embarrassing when people say, \"Hey, that\u0027s my forum,\" \"Hey, that\u0027s my repository,\" \"Hey, that\u0027s my document.\" You\u0027re accessing it without the owner\u0027s permission. If you want to improve, you have to get rid of the feeling of ownership of something that doesn\u0027t belong to you.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c!-- /wp:paragraph --\u003e",
